<title>JAPAN: Tokyo Seimitsu's shares rise on share announcement. [CORRECTED 2:35 GMT]</title>
<headline>Tokyo Seimitsu's shares rise on share announcement. [CORRECTED 2:35 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Tokyo Seimitsu Co Ltd rose sharply on Thursday morning in Tokyo due to the company's announcement on Wednesday it would buy back its own shares.</p>
<p>(Corrects to show announcement was about share repurchase, not the introduction of a stock option scheme).</p>
<p>By 0032 GMT, Tokyo Seimitsu's shares were up 110 yen at 2,880 yen.  </p>
<p>The maker of semiconductor-manufacturing equipment said on Wednesday it planned to buy back three billion yen worth of its shares or one million in total.</p>
</text>
